# Prepares the built fixture druid-shoulder-metal-seed7-opt0822 for the checks that load it (bd inc-10v7f).
# The old fixture, a .sav, held this state: wizard mode on, and a plain iron long sword on the L. Shoulder
# (inc-d9gk). Expertise makes a held weapon's parry value count toward Defense Class; a Wood Elf is proficient
# with a long sword, so its parry modifier of 3 is not cut. Starting gear is nonmetal.
# Ruling V7-1: a fixture holds only the created character, so the checks that need the state make it here.
@while "more --" SPACE
w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*9
@until "long sword" DOWN
ENTER
e SPACE
b SPACE
d
# Drop what the swaps left in the air (the old character's quarterstaff; the built one's scythe).
f SPACE d
@expect "L. Shoulder  :long sword"
@expect "R. Shoulder  :Empty"
@expect "Weapon Hand  :elven darkwood short bow"
ESC
